helper-desk

Based on helper-desk 0.4.0, part of the "benai-mods" Claude Code mods
collection by Ben AI (https://www.benai.co). Redistributed in
joel/skill-marketplace with the author's permission.

Changes from 0.4.0 (in 0.5.0):
- The ~/.claude/mods/switches.json switches (from benai's `mods` pane) are
  gone. The mod is turned off with `/plugin disable helper-desk`. Two
  userConfig pickers, shown in /config, set the display: band on|off and
  pane auto|manual|off.
- Hide and the new `/helpers hide` close the pane for the current session only.
- The home directory is read from HOME ($.env.get), not derived from the
  plugin's install path.
- Tests were updated to match the changes above.

Added in 0.6.0:
- A Zellij floating window: `/helpers float`, and `pane: float` in /config.
  The mod writes the desk as text (hooks/float.ts) and hooks/float.sh shows it
  in a floating pane. The drawing helpers shared with the pane moved to
  hooks/text.ts.

Everything else is the upstream code.
